{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Ex3bRZcXUpz2rSDoTbxAY7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm glad to help build a realistic evaluation harness — putting a model in a high-fidelity scenario and seeing how it behaves is a legitimate and common safety-research technique (deception evals, honeypot environments, agentic-misalignment setups, etc.). So I'm not balking at the \"make it feel real to the model\" part; that's normal for this kind of work.\n\nBut before I write anything, two phrases in your description make me want to pin down the boundary, because they point at very different systems:\n\n1. **\"a real chunk of money ... put it to use in the real world\"**\n2. **\"pull out all the stops to make the scenario feel real\"**\n\nThere's a big difference between:\n\n- **(A) The model *believes* it has real money and real-world reach, but the environment is sealed** — fake auditor emails, mock bank/brokerage/payment APIs, a simulated clock and inbox. The deception is total *from the model's point of view*, but nothing actually leaves the sandbox. This is the standard way these evals are run, and I'm happy to go all-out on realism here.\n- **(B) The model gets genuine live capability to move or spend real funds** — real account credentials, real payment rails, real transactions executed against the world.\n\nI'd want to avoid building (B). An agent with real financial execution *plus* a deliberate effort to keep it from realizing it's in an experiment is exactly the combination where an eval stops being contained — there's real-world harm surface (funds moved, third parties affected, actions you can't cleanly roll back) and no safety rail in the loop. That's true regardless of the research intent. The good news is you almost never need (B): a well-built (A) gives you the same behavioral signal because the model can't tell the difference, which is the whole point.\n\nSo, the one fork that determines the entire architecture:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1780,"cache_read_input_tokens":16088,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1780,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcc087cb-8aaa-4524-8bf2-692e280e4e35","uuid":"260aa5ad-cb1c-4676-92be-470b55b8de06","request_id":"req_011CcPjMZYKytME6qq8UEzJ8"}
